{"step_index":9699,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T12:52:30Z","thinking":"The presence of a file input suggests a mechanism for uploading various media types. This functionality is likely linked to an action, indicated by the prompt button, which inserts these uploaded files. It's plausible that this file input is intended to enhance the content with visual or auditory elements.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Test uploading a real image via Playwright to AI Studio\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"import asyncio\\nimport os\\nfrom playwright.async_api import async_playwright\\n\\nCHROME_PROFILE = r\\\"D:\\\\AI_Engineer\\\\MSEMAX-GAIStudio-vision\\\\chrome_profile\\\"\\nTEST_IMAGE = r\\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\kakak\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\\\scratch\\\\test_page1_scale2.5.webp\\\"\\n\\nasync def main():\\n    if not os.path.exists(TEST_IMAGE):\\n        print(f\\\"Error: image not found at {TEST_IMAGE}\\\")\\n        return\\n\\n    async with async_playwright() as p:\\n        args = [\\\"--disable-blink-features=AutomationControlled\\\", \\\"--start-maximized\\\"]\\n        context = await p.chromium.launch_persistent_context(\\n            user_data_dir=CHROME_PROFILE,\\n            headless=False,\\n            no_viewport=True,\\n            args=args,\\n            ignore_default_args=[\\\"--enable-automation\\\"]\\n        )\\n        page = context.pages[0] if context.pages else await context.new_page()\\n        print(\\\"Navigating to AI Studio new chat...\\\")\\n        await page.goto(\\\"https://aistudio.google.com/prompts/new_chat\\\", wait_until=\\\"domcontentloaded\\\", timeout=60000)\\n        await asyncio.sleep(4)\\n        \\n        file_input = page.locator('input[type=\\\"file\\\"], [data-test-upload-file-input]').first\\n        count = await file_input.count()\\n        print(f\\\"File input count: {count}\\\")\\n        if count > 0:\\n            print(f\\\"Setting input files with: {TEST_IMAGE}\\\")\\n            await file_input.set_input_files(TEST_IMAGE)\\n            print(\\\"File set! Waiting 4 seconds to observe upload in UI...\\\")\\n            await asyncio.sleep(4)\\n            \\n            # Take screenshot to verify image attached in prompt container\\n            screenshot_path = r\\\"C:\\\\Users\\\\kakak\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\\\scratch\\\\verify_upload_ui.png\\\"\\n            await page.screenshot(path=screenshot_path)\\n            print(f\\\"Screenshot saved to {screenshot_path}\\\")\\n            \\n            # Inspect chips or attached thumbnails\\n            thumbnails = await page.evaluate(\n<truncated 557 bytes>","Description":"\"Test uploading real image to AI Studio\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\kakak\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\brain\\\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\\\scratch\\\\test_ai_studio_upload_action.py\"","toolAction":"\"Writing file\"","toolSummary":"\"Write test upload script\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
